  "foaf:name": "Blue Economy Network for ECOPs in LAC",
  "sdo:name": "Blue Economy Network for ECOPs in LAC",
  "sdo:description": "The Blue Economy Capacity Network for Latin America and the Caribbean: Empowering ECOPs for Ocean Sustainability (BLUE-LAC-ECOPS)  is a multi-year project that aims to establish an international network of Vocational Education and Training (VET) institutions and secondary schools, focusing on ocean entrepreneurship, sustainability, and blue economy innovation. The project empowers Early Career Ocean Professionals (ECOPs) and local communities to co-create solutions for sustainable ocean economies in the region. Key components include capacity building, innovation and action (e.g., Ocean Climathon), networking and policy dialogue (Blue Economy Conference), and the establishment of a regional knowledge hub. The project will produce training packages, youth innovation pipelines, and policy work, ensuring long-lasting impact and continued collaboration across Latin America and the Caribbean.",
